WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
After Zhuge Liang passed away, the court of Shu Han grew quieter day by day.

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:10.070
The Later Lord Liu Shan sat on the dragon throne, brow deeply furrowed, unable to make up his mind.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.588
He gazed into the distance, his heart full of worry and unease.

00:00:13.938 --> 00:00:21.810
In the north, the great army of Wei began to move. The veteran Deng Ai and Zhong Hui led their soldiers toward Shu Han.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.120
The two armies moved separately, closing in on Shu Han step by step.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:36.838
Deng Ai led his elite soldiers over mountains and ridges, slipping through Yinping. The snowy peaks were high and perilous, and everyone pressed forward step by step.

00:00:37.188 --> 00:00:41.676
On the mountain road the cold wind cut to the bone, and the soldiers supported each other as they advanced.

00:00:42.026 --> 00:00:46.946
The gates of Chengdu slowly opened, and Liu Shan walked out of the city and chose to surrender.

00:00:47.296 --> 00:00:52.696
The people in the city were quiet — there was no fire of war, and no sound of weeping.

00:00:53.046 --> 00:00:58.638
The banner of Shu Han slowly came down. Under the sunset, an era quietly came to an end.

00:00:58.988 --> 00:01:02.276
After forty-three years, Shu Han passed into history.

